{"episodes":{"201618":"A cold front tracked across Eastern North Carolina on the evening of the thirty-first. Out ahead of this front, scattered showers and thunderstorms developed and tracked south-eastwards, mainly impacting the waters south of Oregon Inlet. A few of these thunderstorms became strong to severe in nature bringing a strong and damaging wind threat within the strongest storms.","201746":"Scattered showers and thunderstorms formed mainly over Mono, southern Lyon and southern Mineral counties with several hundred recorded lightning strikes and strong outflow winds during the afternoon.","201871":"A few slow moving severe thunderstorms developed over the mountains and tracked eastward into the Interstate 25 and Interstate 80 corridors during the afternoon of June 1st. These thunderstorms were slow moving under weak shear and took a while to become severe.","202403":"Thunderstorms produced damaging winds across portions of SE Texas.","202443":"A band of marginally severe thunderstorms moved from northern into central Oklahoma during the late evening of the 31st into early morning of June 1st, producing a report of thunderstorm wind damage in Grant County.","202670":"Scattered thunderstorms, originating during the late evening hours 31 May, continued to impact portions of central Oklahoma during the early morning hours of the 1st. A few reports of hail were received.","202789":"Showers and thunderstorms brought gusty outflow winds.","203193":"On the afternoon of June 1st, an outflow boundary from morning thunderstorms, combined with a strong shortwave trough moving south from the Southern Plains into North Texas, created a focus for thunderstorm development. These storms began near the I-20 corridor and moved south throughout the afternoon, eventually dissipating over Central Texas by evening. The most significant severe weather event associated with this system was large hail, up to 3, in Parker and Tarrant counties.","203208":"A surface cold front digging south from Virginia, coupled to a deep trough of low pressure over the eastern United States, led to a line of scattered thunderstorms during the afternoon and evening, mainly across the southern Piedmont, Sandhills, and southern Coastal Plain of central North Carolina. Isolated damaging winds were observed in Moore, Randolph, and Sampson Counties.","204203":"A storm late in the evening on May 31st brough quarter sized hail to Atchison, KS.","204276":"Northwest flow remained over the area, and allowed for strong to severe storms to develops across southern portions of the region.","204277":"Broad ridge with weak disturbances within the flow was in place over the area, allowing for messy strong to severe storms to develop.","204431":"A frontal boundary stalled near Lake Okeechobee while a mid-level disturbance allowed for strong to severe thunderstorms to develop on the morning and early afternoon of June 1, 2025.","204747":"River flooding continued from May into June along the Cache, White, Black, and Ouachita Rivers.","204837":"An isolated thunderstorm developed over Big Pine Key and moved east-northeast over Vaca Key, producing isolated gale-force wind gusts.  A stalled frontal boundary was positioned across mainland south Florida.","204861":"Isolated thunderstorms developed over upstate South Carolina during the late afternoon and evening. One of the storms produced brief damaging wind gusts in Greenville County.","204863":"Isolated thunderstorms developed over the North Carolina Piedmont during the late afternoon and evening. A couple of the storms produced brief damaging wind gusts in Mecklenburg County."},"events":[{"begin":"2025-06-01T00:05Z","county":"Neuse And Bay Rivers","deaths":0,"end":"2025-06-01T00:05Z","endLat":35.0095,"endLon":-76.665,"episode":201618,"id":1252229,"injuries":0,"lat":35.0095,"location":"2 SE Oriental","lon":-76.665,"magnitude":45.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","narrative":"Wind gust occurred as thunderstorms moved through the waters near t